				<title>Greek vs Roman names</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-891139/prometheus-labs-hub#post-3641773</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 28 Nov 2017 23:36:41 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>DrHematite</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3350227</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I realize this is quite late in the life of this GoI, but I was wondering why the hiring packet uses the Roman name &quot;Saturn&quot; as opposed to the Greek name &quot;Cronus&quot; or &quot;Kronos&quot;, when every other deity is represented using their Greek names (Prometheus, Gaea, Ouranos/Uranus and Zeus, as opposed to Prometheus, Terra, Caelus and Jupiter)?</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
