					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-891139#post-2056590</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-891139/prometheus-labs-hub#post-2056590</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 23 Jun 2014 00:55:34 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>A Random Day</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1841781</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Prometheus Labs' stance on anomalous objects is that they simply do not adhere to what is considered current science. Like their blurb states, &quot;one thousand years ago it was considered current science that the sun rotated around the Earth&quot;.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-891139#post-2056551</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-891139/prometheus-labs-hub#post-2056551</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 22 Jun 2014 23:47:01 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Chaoseed</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>479761</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I really like this. You definitely get the feeling of a big company, a company that prides itself on innovation, yet at the same time has serious paperwork where it counts.</p> <p>(My <em>one</em> criticism would be that it almost seems TOO normal&#8230;the key thing about SCP, as I see it, is that these objects simply cannot be understood by current science. I feel like there should be some concession to &quot;anomalousness&quot; in the documents. Although, &quot;the mental web and teleportation were invented&quot; is nice!)</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
